      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The definition says, “No element of H^{-1}(Ω) is a distribution here.” Counterexample: over ℝ on Ω=(0,1), F(v)=∫₀¹v dx is in H^{-1} by Cauchy–Schwarz, and on C_c^∞(0,1) it is exactly the regular distribution u₁(φ)=∫₀¹φ dx. The dependency `def-regular-distribution-from-a-locally-integrable-function` defines this pairing, and `thm-locally-integrable-functions-embed-in-distributions` identifies it with an element of 𝒟′. The sentence could say H^{-1} is defined by its action on Sobolev classes, but its categorical negation is false.",
